[{:db/id "q-110547/selection/539e6b03f729a9490b66c1a3e49d7a01e331e0240d259c383e1cbf826f13dc38" :answer/id #uuid "cd41f161-22b4-5482-8a38-d6003cd0d5ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547/selection/652b9a572fc71e399fc0e4beec9365acae9514d897e524c329ba17dddced4564" :answer/id #uuid "baca1430-7cb5-56ac-956c-b98b2494f449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547/selection/0d1e2ba5c23c72dde2b832cbd864af1344141b675ac0efe64f5f8b051dbbc1da" :answer/id #uuid "c6cbf6c7-5820-58c1-9cec-9bed5e3a4fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547/selection/4a86b974ba6c78946b7cf1f7a681dd9af72446cacd83fac448adeb8f5081ec56" :answer/id #uuid "2fa92159-18e4-51cd-bde2-ee8ad104673f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547/selection/f2d71b44183b137af443a2bb566e2ecd7503e10f04ba68c2d8361ea216f72242" :answer/id #uuid "74811bd2-a53c-58af-9ca9-8871c7520ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e979991d-f405-5f97-a52d-cbdf219572f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110547/selection/539e6b03f729a9490b66c1a3e49d7a01e331e0240d259c383e1cbf826f13dc38" :answer-field/choices ["q-110547/selection/539e6b03f729a9490b66c1a3e49d7a01e331e0240d259c383e1cbf826f13dc38" "q-110547/selection/652b9a572fc71e399fc0e4beec9365acae9514d897e524c329ba17dddced4564" "q-110547/selection/0d1e2ba5c23c72dde2b832cbd864af1344141b675ac0efe64f5f8b051dbbc1da" "q-110547/selection/4a86b974ba6c78946b7cf1f7a681dd9af72446cacd83fac448adeb8f5081ec56" "q-110547/selection/f2d71b44183b137af443a2bb566e2ecd7503e10f04ba68c2d8361ea216f72242"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110547" :question/id #uuid "6ce89dab-2573-58ef-b1ae-998929df8c15" :question/math-academy-id "q-110547" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${2}^{4x}={3}^{1-x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{4x} & ={3}^{1-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{4x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{1-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)=(1-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =(1-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ x(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110547/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc9469a-e2ca-55ba-b05a-b0be37384f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-233244/field-1/7e00aa9c4013e1cc481991fb87b6470c42d7ad6df39b8bd70b39cf1f3a23fbde" :answer/id #uuid "457e08fc-0e12-51ae-bf10-2005db223d04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\ln(5)+3\\ln(7)}{\\ln(5)+2\\ln(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-233244/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f85bce8d-8241-50a8-8dc7-3a156995ef7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-233244/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4542e3b-9561-594b-b6a3-ccc39c211265" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-233244/field-1/7e00aa9c4013e1cc481991fb87b6470c42d7ad6df39b8bd70b39cf1f3a23fbde" :answer-field/choices ["q-233244/field-1/7e00aa9c4013e1cc481991fb87b6470c42d7ad6df39b8bd70b39cf1f3a23fbde" "q-233244/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-233244" :question/id #uuid "1bb6b417-40c6-590c-a34f-11b86676b4c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-233244" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${5}^{x-2}={7}^{3-2x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x-2} & ={7}^{3-2x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{x-2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{3-2x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)=(3-2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =(3-2x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-233244/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc9469a-e2ca-55ba-b05a-b0be37384f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-233244"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242902/field-1/7e723a4c345d1b302e044dcb2e8de441b68d2894a1cb045cca9cbb4fe8e33e46" :answer/id #uuid "a4635ab6-c06d-59a5-a5d1-b19ecc37ab1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\ln(2)-2}{1-\\ln(2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242902/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "531ee5d0-a628-5849-860b-4cc02b16d934" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-242902/field-1/7e723a4c345d1b302e044dcb2e8de441b68d2894a1cb045cca9cbb4fe8e33e46" :answer-field/choices ["q-242902/field-1/7e723a4c345d1b302e044dcb2e8de441b68d2894a1cb045cca9cbb4fe8e33e46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242902" :question/id #uuid "7c0698ed-83ff-5702-9102-b20873016600" :question/math-academy-id "q-242902" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{x+2}={2}^{x+3}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+2} & ={2}^{x+3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x+2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx+2=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+3}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx+2=(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =(x+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x+2 & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2}{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-242902/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eb24b54-bdb8-5269-bd38-d346a52bbc6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242904/field-1/9e26728215d38c0d3b8c8fa977d5cacdcce83772373a15d578012408d24dd461" :answer/id #uuid "0999f33a-b3b9-54af-9024-42bac13649f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\ln(2)}{2-\\ln(9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242904/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "b0a7d883-5f10-5d2c-baa7-a69df3455bae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242904/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfff3ad-889e-5faa-88dd-7cf4136957f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-242904/field-1/9e26728215d38c0d3b8c8fa977d5cacdcce83772373a15d578012408d24dd461" :answer-field/choices ["q-242904/field-1/9e26728215d38c0d3b8c8fa977d5cacdcce83772373a15d578012408d24dd461" "q-242904/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242904" :question/id #uuid "eb2badcc-b8ec-5da1-a517-670e53be7625" :question/math-academy-id "q-242904" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, determine the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${e}^{2x-2}=2\\cdot {9}^{x}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x-2} & =2\\cdot {9}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x-2}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {9}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n2x-2=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {9}^{x}).\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power and product laws of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({9}^{x}) \\\\ 2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) \\\\ 2x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9) & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)) & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ x & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-242904/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eb24b54-bdb8-5269-bd38-d346a52bbc6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection/1e0594fab11d2ec8dcf124959707aef24ad7ed10ca5da8be57d643015d27e759" :answer/id #uuid "e4ae7470-01ca-59f3-86f4-df8c4e429830" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection/24f35962d7522cd06503b2539cc44e714d5c88e131ceb2002c06661de4b13523" :answer/id #uuid "3a35dffe-0735-5880-bc32-ac6e9787bb2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection/ce6c14343bf2b9b823163dde03248669fc0d9a3afb9a648d977d91b7352f6a62" :answer/id #uuid "7cc5e5f5-3265-5fd1-b3f0-b4f8a8a62f83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection/35f710cef1ed2aaa02d2258cfafeed787b7b3db1539ce95ac1f829971a51f683" :answer/id #uuid "28b646c6-b315-57c9-97fa-fcb18345e6d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection/cb82c74c37035f510f9879de0c0d606edd4f321b9d6b39f63d02c276f3884973" :answer/id #uuid "3178b431-d1d7-54ac-b56b-4058921713ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "631d464a-580d-594e-a38e-b389a1ced2fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-242922/selection/cb82c74c37035f510f9879de0c0d606edd4f321b9d6b39f63d02c276f3884973" :answer-field/choices ["q-242922/selection/1e0594fab11d2ec8dcf124959707aef24ad7ed10ca5da8be57d643015d27e759" "q-242922/selection/24f35962d7522cd06503b2539cc44e714d5c88e131ceb2002c06661de4b13523" "q-242922/selection/ce6c14343bf2b9b823163dde03248669fc0d9a3afb9a648d977d91b7352f6a62" "q-242922/selection/35f710cef1ed2aaa02d2258cfafeed787b7b3db1539ce95ac1f829971a51f683" "q-242922/selection/cb82c74c37035f510f9879de0c0d606edd4f321b9d6b39f63d02c276f3884973"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242922" :question/id #uuid "59428ee5-d2e3-5609-8db7-0bd07aac8005" :question/math-academy-id "q-242922" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${2}^{5x-1}={7}^{3-x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{5x-1} & ={7}^{3-x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{5x-1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{3-x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify both sides of the equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =(3-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =(3-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ 5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ 5x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7) \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-242922/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dc9469a-e2ca-55ba-b05a-b0be37384f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242922"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
